<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muhammad V of Kelantan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1969">1969</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muhammad V of Kelantan has been sultan of Kelantan, in north-eastern Peninsular Malaysia, since 2010. In 2016 he was elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yang-di-pertuan-agong">Yang di-Pertuan Agong</a>, the king of Malaysia, under the country's rotating monarchy. He abdicated as king in January 2019, the first Malaysian monarch to do so, but remained sultan of Kelantan.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/muhammad-v-of-kelantan.jpg" alt="Muhammad V of Kelantan" width="320" height="396" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: RTV Kelantan · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sultan_Muhammad_V_dari_Kelantan_pada_tahun_2013.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
